# {{ .Group.Name }} Skill Package

Generated by `opencli` for `{{ .App.Name }} {{ .Group.Name }}`.

This directory is meant to be handed to product, business, engineering, and QA owners for completion. The generated files contain CLI facts from the API or MCP description; they do not know the real business workflow yet.

## Directory

```text
skills/{{ skillName .Group }}/
├── SKILL.md
├── README.md
├── assets/
│   └── demo-request.json
├── references/
│   ├── command-routing.md
│   ├── workflows.md
│   └── production-checklist.md
└── generation-report.md
```

## File Purposes

| File | Owner | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SKILL.md` | Skill maintainer | Agent entrypoint. Keep trigger rules, hard safety rules, command index, and short workflow summaries here. |
| `README.md` | Everyone | Explains the package structure and handoff process. |
| `assets/demo-request.json` | Engineering + QA | Valid placeholder JSON file for `--data @file` examples, demos, and manual request-body editing. |
| `references/command-routing.md` | Product + skill maintainer | Maps user intent to the correct generated CLI command. Fill this before relying on natural-language routing. |
| `references/workflows.md` | Product + engineering + QA | Defines real multi-command business flows, including confirmation and read-back checks. |
| `references/production-checklist.md` | QA + maintainer | Acceptance checklist before the skill is treated as production-ready. |
| `generation-report.md` | Skill maintainer | Lists missing descriptions detected in the source API/MCP input. |

## Completion Order

1. Run `{{ .App.Name }} {{ .Group.Name }} --help` and each command `--help` to verify the generated command surface.
2. Use `--data @assets/demo-request.json` as the starting request body for JSON commands.
3. Review `generation-report.md` and decide whether to fix the source API/MCP description or fill the skill manually.
4. Fill `references/command-routing.md` with common user requests, synonyms, and commands to avoid.
5. Fill `references/workflows.md` with the top 3-5 business workflows.
6. Move only the shortest, most important routing and workflow rules back into `SKILL.md`.
7. Validate with `references/production-checklist.md`.

